## 6. From confidence to High, Medium, Low

> **In one sentence:** $C$ sets the tier, two guardrails can lower it, and every tier comes with its main driver.

### The tiers

| Confidence $C$ | Tier |
|:-:|:-:|
| 0.90 or more | 🟢 High |
| 0.70 up to 0.90 | 🟡 Medium |
| Below 0.70 | 🔴 Low |

These cutoffs are **illustrative starting points**, set properly in shadow mode ([section 12](#12-rollout-plan)).

### Two guardrails

Each guardrail can only *lower* the tier, and caps it at 🟡 Medium:

| Guardrail | Rule | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Thin neighborhood** | Fewer than 30 comparable homes in the home's r5 cell | The neighborhood estimate is mostly borrowed from far away, so we can't vouch for it |
| **Extreme outlier** | \$/sqft more than 3 spreads from the neighborhood center: $\lvert z \rvert > 3$, where $z = \ln(\text{\$/sqft} / e^{\hat\mu}) / \sigma_N$ | When Verisk's range is very tight, the pull is small, so even a wild outlier barely moves $C$. This catches it. |

### The main driver: a confidence waterfall

To explain *why* a quote landed where it did, build the confidence one signal at a time:

| Step | What's included |
|---|---|
| **Start** | 100% |
| **Final MERC range** | Verisk's precision only: the best this quote could possibly score |
| **+ Property Confidence Score** | Adds the leftover data risk |
| **+ Neighborhood estimate** | Adds the neighborhood pull |
| **+ Prefill vs. final** | Adds the "member was wrong" version, giving the final $C$ |

The step with the biggest drop is the **main driver**. It turns into a plain-English reason:

| Main driver | Example reason |
|---|---|
| Final MERC range | Verisk's range is wide (±9%) |
| Property Confidence Score | Verisk's data on this home is rated 3 of 5 |
| Neighborhood estimate | \$154/sq ft vs. \$184 typical nearby (−16%) |
| Prefill vs. final | Member changes lowered MERC 25%, below Verisk's prefill range |

### What to do with each tier (suggested)

| Tier | Suggested action |
|:-:|---|
| 🟢 High | None |
| 🟡 Medium | Log the reason; optionally include it in underwriting review |
| 🔴 Low | Route to underwriting review, or prioritize for post-bind inspection |

