## 11. Contract checkpoints

> **In one sentence:** everything here uses Verisk output from real quotes, as returned, with two aggregations that should be confirmed.

| Use of Verisk output | Type | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Final MERC and range (quote-flow step 5) | Per quote, as returned | Already in use |
| Prefill MERC and range (quote-flow step 2) | Per quote, on Verisk's own attributes for a real address | Confirm it's included in the prefill response. If it needs its own call, that call prices a real house as Verisk describes it, not a hypothetical one. |
| Property Confidence Score | Per quote, as returned | Already in use in the attribute model |
| Neighborhood \$/sqft reference | Stored MERCs aggregated across the book | Confirmed acceptable by the team |
| Calibration of $\sigma_D$ by PCS | Stored prefill and final MERCs aggregated across the book | **Confirm it's in the same category as the neighborhood reference.** If not, keep the judgment starting values and validate with attribute data only. |

> ⚖️ **Design principle:** no what-if calls, no designed studies, and no model with MERC as the outcome. MERC is only ever *looked up* or *compared*.

