## Appendix A: Notation cheat sheet

| Symbol | Plain English | Comes from |
|:-:|---|---|
| $s$ | Log change from prefill MERC to final MERC | Signals 1 and 2 |
| $\sigma_V$ | Verisk's precision: the range as a log-scale spread | Signal 2 (or 1, for the "member was wrong" version) |
| $\sigma_D$ | Leftover data risk | Signal 3, via the PCS table |
| $\sigma$ | Total uncertainty of one version: $\sqrt{\sigma_V^2 + \sigma_D^2}$ | Signals 1–3 |
| $N$ | Neighborhood estimate: typical \$/sqft nearby × square footage | Signal 4 |
| $\sigma_N$ | Neighborhood spread | Signal 4 |
| $w$ | Neighborhood pull: $\sigma^2 / (\sigma^2 + \sigma_N^2)$ | Signals 2–4 |
| $\delta$ | Center of the true cost, as a log offset from the quote | Signals 1–4 |
| $q$ | Chance the member's changes are wrong | Inspections |
| $c$ | Chance of landing in tolerance for one version | Section 5, step 3 |
| $C$ | MERC confidence: the weighted average of the two versions | Section 5, step 4 |
| $\tau_{\text{under}}, \tau_{\text{over}}$ | How far too low or too high the MERC may be | Business decision |
| $z$ | How many neighborhood spreads the home's \$/sqft sits from typical | Signal 4 (guardrail) |

